  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>. The system of linear equations<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />is inconsistent for :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "exactly one positive value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "exactly one negative value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "every value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "exactly two values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here, we will use Cramer&#39;s Rule according to which,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;if the system of linear equations is inconsistent.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#955;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
